cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StableRCWA in published work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: StableRCWA
abstract: >-
  Header-only C++17 implementation of rigorous coupled-wave analysis (RCWA, the Fourier modal method)
  for 1-D and 2-D periodic gratings, stable at high truncation orders. Includes conical incidence with
  full Jones matrices, six-component near fields and phase, a JSON command-line interface and a local web GUI.
authors:
  - family-names: Ding
    given-names: Xinhui
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aikkkkko/StableRCWA"
keywords:
  - RCWA
  - rigorous coupled-wave analysis
  - Fourier modal method
  - diffraction grating
  - photonics
  - computational electromagnetics
